{"title": "How much chicken per person? A size guide for Christmas and parties", "seo_title": "How Much Chicken Per Person? Size Guide and Calculator | Colonel Clucks", "description": "How much chicken per person for Christmas or a party? Use our calculator and portion tables, compare whole and cut, and get roasting times and safe storage tips from a Jos broiler farm.", "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} -->\n<p class=\"lead\">Short answer: plan on about 450 g of whole bird per adult for a main meal, 300 g if there are lots of other dishes and 600 g for hungry guests. Use the calculator and tables below to pick the right size.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"byline\"} -->\n<p class=\"byline\">Written by the <strong>Colonel Clucks team</strong>, Jos, Plateau State · Updated 21 November 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"answer\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group answer\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tag\"} -->\n<p class=\"tag\">The short version</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rules of thumb for chicken portions</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Chicken is the main dish:</strong> plan on about 450 g of whole bird per adult.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>A party with many other dishes:</strong> about 300 g per adult.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Hungry guests or you want leftovers:</strong> about 600 g per adult.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Children under 12:</strong> about half an adult portion.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Weights are bird weight with bones.</strong> That is why they are bigger than the meat on a plate.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"toc\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group toc\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"toc-title\"} -->\n<p class=\"toc-title\">On this page</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#calculator\">Chicken calculator</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#portions\">Portion sizes</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#guests\">How much for 2 to 50 adults</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#choice\">Whole or cut for each dish</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#cook\">Roasting times</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#store\">Storing, thawing and leftovers</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#mistakes\">Common mistakes</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#method\">How we made this guide</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#faq\">Questions</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Free tool</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"calculator\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"calculator\">Chicken calculator</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tell us who is eating and how hungry they are. The calculator works out the weight you need and suggests a mix of our whole bird sizes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<form class=\"calc\" onsubmit=\"return false\">\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div><label for=\"cAdults\">Adults</label><input id=\"cAdults\" inputmode=\"numeric\" max=\"150\" min=\"0\" type=\"number\" value=\"8\"/></div>\n<div><label for=\"cKids\">Children under 12</label><input id=\"cKids\" inputmode=\"numeric\" max=\"150\" min=\"0\" type=\"number\" value=\"2\"/></div>\n<div><label for=\"cAppetite\">Meal type</label>\n<select id=\"cAppetite\">\n<option value=\"0.3\">Party with many other dishes (300 g)</option>\n<option selected=\"\" value=\"0.45\">Chicken is the main dish (450 g)</option>\n<option value=\"0.6\">Hungry guests or leftovers (600 g)</option>\n</select></div>\n</div>\n<div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"result\" id=\"cResult\"></div>\n</form><script>\n(function(){\n  var SIZES=[35,30,25,15], NAMES=[\"3.5 kg\",\"3 kg\",\"2.5 kg\",\"1.5 kg\"];\n  var $=function(id){return document.getElementById(id)};\n  function best(need){\n    var b=null;\n    for(var a=0;a<=20;a++)for(var x=0;x<=6;x++)for(var c=0;c<=6;c++)for(var d=0;d<=6;d++){\n      var tot=a*35+x*30+c*25+d*15; if(tot<need)continue;\n      var over=tot-need, n=a+x+c+d;\n      if(!b||over<b.over||(over===b.over&&n<b.n))b={over:over,n:n,c:[a,x,c,d],tot:tot};\n    }\n    return b;\n  }\n  function run(){\n    var adults=Math.max(0,Math.min(150,parseInt($(\"cAdults\").value,10)||0));\n    var kids=Math.max(0,Math.min(150,parseInt($(\"cKids\").value,10)||0));\n    var per=parseFloat($(\"cAppetite\").value);\n    var needKg=(adults+kids*0.5)*per;\n    var out=$(\"cResult\");\n    if(needKg<=0){out.innerHTML=\"<h3>Your answer</h3><p>Add at least one adult or child.</p>\";return;}\n    var need=Math.ceil(needKg*10-1e-9);\n    var r=best(need);\n    if(!r){out.innerHTML=\"<h3>Your answer</h3><p>That is a big event. Please message us on WhatsApp and we will plan it with you.</p>\";return;}\n    var parts=[];for(var i=0;i<4;i++)if(r.c[i])parts.push(r.c[i]+\" &times; \"+NAMES[i]+\" whole\");\n    out.innerHTML=\"<h3>Your answer</h3><p>You need about <span class=\\\"big\\\">\"+needKg.toFixed(1)+\" kg</span> of bird.</p>\"+\n      \"<p><strong>Suggested whole-bird order:</strong> \"+parts.join(\" + \")+\" (total \"+(r.tot/10).toFixed(1)+\" kg).</p>\"+\n      \"<p>Prefer cut birds? Each cut bird is about 1.5 to 1.9 kg, so about \"+Math.ceil(needKg/1.7)+\" cut bird\"+(Math.ceil(needKg/1.7)===1?\"\":\"s\")+\" would cover it.</p>\"+\n      \"<p><a href=\\\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\\\">Place this order with our online order form</a></p>\";\n  }\n  [\"cAdults\",\"cKids\",\"cAppetite\"].forEach(function(id){$(id).addEventListener(\"input\",run);$(id).addEventListener(\"change\",run);});\n  run();\n})();\n</script>\n<!-- /wp:html --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Portions</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"portions\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"portions\">Portion sizes per person</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Per adult</th><th>Per child under 12</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Party with many other dishes</th><td>300 g</td><td>150 g</td><td>Jollof, fried rice, salad, plantain and other meats on the table</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Chicken is the main dish</th><td>450 g</td><td>225 g</td><td>A family Christmas lunch with rice and sides</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hungry guests or leftovers wanted</th><td>600 g</td><td>300 g</td><td>Big eaters, men's gathering, or you want cold chicken the next day</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Chicken per person (bird weight, bones included)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Our own planning figures, not an official standard. See how we made this guide below.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Quick lookup</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"guests\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"guests\">How much chicken for 2 to 50 adults</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Find your number of adults, then read across. The last two columns show the closest mix of our whole bird sizes for a normal main-dish meal, with the smallest amount of waste.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Adults</th><th>Party (300 g)</th><th>Main dish (450 g)</th><th>Hungry (600 g)</th><th>Suggested whole birds (main dish)</th><th>Total weight</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">2 adults</th><td>0.6 kg</td><td>0.9 kg</td><td>1.2 kg</td><td>1 × 1.5 kg</td><td>1.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 adults</th><td>1.2 kg</td><td>1.8 kg</td><td>2.4 kg</td><td>1 × 2.5 kg</td><td>2.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">6 adults</th><td>1.8 kg</td><td>2.7 kg</td><td>3.6 kg</td><td>1 × 3 kg</td><td>3 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">8 adults</th><td>2.4 kg</td><td>3.6 kg</td><td>4.8 kg</td><td>1 × 2.5 kg + 1 × 1.5 kg</td><td>4 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">10 adults</th><td>3 kg</td><td>4.5 kg</td><td>6 kg</td><td>1 × 3 kg + 1 × 1.5 kg</td><td>4.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">15 adults</th><td>4.5 kg</td><td>6.8 kg</td><td>9 kg</td><td>2 × 3.5 kg</td><td>7 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">20 adults</th><td>6 kg</td><td>9 kg</td><td>12 kg</td><td>3 × 3 kg</td><td>9 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">30 adults</th><td>9 kg</td><td>13.5 kg</td><td>18 kg</td><td>3 × 3.5 kg + 1 × 3 kg</td><td>13.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">50 adults</th><td>15 kg</td><td>22.5 kg</td><td>30 kg</td><td>3 × 3.5 kg + 4 × 3 kg</td><td>22.5 kg</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Chicken needed by number of adults</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Add children at half an adult each. For a party or a hungry crowd, use the calculator above.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Whole or cut</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"choice\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"choice\">Whole or cut: what suits each dish</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Dish</th><th>Best choice</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Roast chicken for the table</th><td>Whole</td><td>You carve it at the table and the skin crisps all over.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Jollof or fried rice with chicken on the side</th><td>Cut</td><td>The pieces fry or grill evenly and portion out easily.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Pepper soup</th><td>Cut</td><td>Bone-in pieces give the broth more flavour.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Chicken stew or sauce</th><td>Cut</td><td>Pieces cook through at the same speed and are easy to serve.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Peppered chicken or grilling</th><td>Cut</td><td>Smaller pieces take marinade well and cook faster.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Boiling a whole bird for stock and shredded meat</th><td>Whole</td><td>One big pot gives you meat and a rich stock.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Which to choose for each dish</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Both are packed to order. You can mix them, for example one whole bird to roast and one cut bird for stew.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Cooking</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"cook\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"cook\">Roasting times by bird size</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A common oven rule is about <strong>20 minutes per 500 g plus 20 minutes</strong> at 180°C. Ovens differ, so use these as a starting point and check the temperature with a meat thermometer.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Bird size</th><th>Approximate time</th><th>Rest before carving</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">1.5 kg</th><td>About 1 hour 20 minutes</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">2.5 kg</th><td>About 2 hours</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 kg</th><td>About 2 hours 20 minutes</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">3.5 kg</th><td>About 2 hours 40 minutes</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Roasting times at 180&amp;deg;C</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"callout\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group callout\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"callout-title\"} -->\n<p class=\"callout-title\"><strong>Is it done?</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Chicken is safe when the thickest part of the thigh reaches at least <strong>74°C (165°F)</strong>. With no thermometer, pierce the thigh: the juices should run clear and the meat should not be pink near the bone. Source: <a href=\"https://chautauqua.cce.cornell.edu/food-nutrition/food-safety-storage/safe-minimum-cooking-temperatures\" rel=\"noopener\">Cornell Cooperative Extension</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Food safety</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"store\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"store\">Storing, thawing and leftovers</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>What to do</th><th>How long</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Raw chicken in the fridge</th><td>Keep it at 4°C or colder, covered, on the lowest shelf so it cannot drip on other food.</td><td>Cook within 2 days</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Raw chicken in the freezer</th><td>Freeze the day you get it, in a sealed bag with the date written on it.</td><td>Best used within 3 months</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Thawing</th><td>Thaw in the fridge, allowing about 24 hours for every 2 kg. Never thaw on the counter.</td><td>Cook within 1 day of thawing</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Cooked leftovers</th><td>Cool, cover and refrigerate within 2 hours of cooking. Reheat until steaming hot all the way through.</td><td>Eat within 2 days</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Power cut</th><td>If the fridge or freezer has been off for several hours, cook the raw chicken the same day.</td><td>Same day</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Storing chicken safely</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">These are cautious, widely used home food-safety guidelines. When in doubt, throw it out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Avoid these</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"mistakes\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"mistakes\">Common mistakes when ordering chicken</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Counting guests but not appetite.</strong> A party buffet and a sit-down lunch need very different amounts.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Forgetting the bones.</strong> A 2.5 kg bird does not give 2.5 kg of meat. Use the bird-weight portions above.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>No fridge space.</strong> A 3.5 kg bird needs a big bowl or tray. Clear space before collection day.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>A pot or oven that is too small.</strong> Check that the bird fits before you order the biggest size.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Washing raw chicken.</strong> Rinsing splashes bacteria around the kitchen. Cooking is what makes chicken safe, so pat it dry instead.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Ordering late.</strong> Christmas weekends fill up fast. Reserve early and pick your day.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Our method</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"method\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"method\">How we made this guide</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We are a small broiler farm in Jos planning how to match our Batch 1 birds to customers' tables. The portion sizes (300 g, 450 g and 600 g of bird weight per adult) are the rules of thumb we use for that planning. They are not an official standard, and your guests may eat more or less.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The temperature, storage and thawing advice follows widely used home food-safety guidance, and we link a source where we quote a number. Roasting times use a common oven rule and will vary with your oven. Where a figure depends on your kitchen, we say so.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"disclose\"} -->\n<p class=\"disclose\"><strong>Full disclosure:</strong> we sell the chicken sizes mentioned on this page. The advice applies to chicken from any seller. We update this page when sizes or advice change.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">FAQ</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"faq\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"faq\">Questions</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>How much chicken do I need for 10 people?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For a normal main-dish meal, about <strong>4.5 kg</strong> of bird for 10 adults. For a party with many other dishes, about 3 kg. For hungry guests, about 6 kg. See the lookup table above.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Is one chicken enough for 4 people?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A 1.5 kg bird feeds about 3 adults as the main dish, or 2 adults and 2 children. For 4 adults, choose the 2.5 kg size.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>How much cooked meat do I get from a whole chicken?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Noticeably less than the raw weight, because bones, skin and cooking losses all take their share. That is why the portions on this page are given as bird weight with bones.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>What size chickens do you sell?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whole birds in 1.5 kg, 2.5 kg, 3 kg and 3.5 kg sizes, and cut birds of about 1.5 to 1.9 kg. We weigh every bird on the sale day and confirm the weight.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Should I wash chicken before cooking?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>No. Washing spreads bacteria onto your sink and worktops. Pat the chicken dry with paper towel and cook it fully.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Can I freeze a whole chicken?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes. Freeze it the day you get it, in a sealed bag, and use it within 3 months for the best quality. Thaw it in the fridge.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Keep reading</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More from the farm</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"related\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group related\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/christmas-chicken-jos/\"><strong>Christmas chicken in Jos</strong></a><br>Sizes, pickup, delivery and how to pre-order.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/about-the-farm/\"><strong>Inside our farm</strong></a><br>Our daily routine, feed plan and Batch 1 facts.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ctaband\",\"align\":\"full\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group ctaband alignfull\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"className\":\"cta-mascot\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full cta-mascot\"><img src=\"{{IMG_HAPPY}}_URL\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Worked out your size?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Batch 1 is ready 18 to 23 December 2026. Order whole or cut birds and pick your day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"cc-btns\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons cc-btns\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-gold\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-gold\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">Place your order</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button -->\n<!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-line\",\"linkTarget\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-line\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086?text=Hello%20Colonel%20Clucks%2C%20I%20have%20a%20question%20about%20ordering%20chicken.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Ask on WhatsApp</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"How much chicken per person? A size guide for Christmas and parties\", \"description\": \"How much chicken per person for Christmas or a party? Use our calculator and portion tables, compare whole and cut, and get roasting times and safe storage tips from a Jos broiler farm.\", \"datePublished\": \"2026-11-21\", \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-21\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/chicken-size-guide